issue_context.body:
Given `H:\` is the empty drive with no file or directory in it, and trying to call `GetDirectories()`:

```c#
namespace EmptyVolume
{
    using System;
    using System.IO;
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            try
            {
                new DirectoryInfo("H:\\").GetDirectories();
                Console.WriteLine("Success!");
            }
            catch (FileNotFoundException e)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("Fail: {0}", e.ToString());
            }
        }
    }
}
```

throws:
```log
Fail: System.IO.FileNotFoundException: Could not find file 'H:\'.
File name: 'H:\'
   at System.IO.Enumeration.FileSystemEnumerator`1.GetData()
   at System.IO.Enumeration.FileSystemEnumerator`1.FindNextEntry()
   at System.IO.Enumeration.FileSystemEnumerator`1.MoveNext()
   at System.Collections.Generic.LargeArrayBuilder`1.AddRange(IEnumerable`1 items)
   at System.Collections.Generic.EnumerableHelpers.ToArray[T](IEnumerable`1 source)
   at System.Linq.Enumerable.ToArray[TSource](IEnumerable`1 source)
   at System.IO.DirectoryInfo.GetDirectories(String searchPattern, EnumerationOptions enumerationOptions)
   at System.IO.DirectoryInfo.GetDirectories()
   at EmptyVolume.Program.Main(String[] args)
```

Tried on _netcoerapp2.1 (2.1.15), netcoerapp 3.1 (3.1.1)_. Also, if network share root volume used to `GetDirectories()`, and it is empty, e.g. `new DirectoryInfo("\\\\serverName\\H$").GetDirectories()`, the same error is thrown. This did not throw on _.net framework (4.6.1 at least)_. Empty root drive means there is no any directory or file, either hidden or system, like "System Volume Information" or "Recycle Bin".

[Related issue, but probably wrong place](https://github.com/dotnet/dotnet-api-docs/issues/3819)/

